From: Matthias Clasen <mclasen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 22 May 2025 14:33:54 -0400
Subject: Fix a crash in the clipping code

When cairo_is_all_clipped returns true, the clip points to the static const
__cairo_clip_all and none of its fields may be changed. This is the upstream
fix referenced by Inkscape issue 5631.

Upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/cairo/cairo/-/commit/1d3347a6904fd4d9a57e4a5e4819de885fce6e46

diff --git a/src/cairo-clip.c b/src/cairo-clip.c
index 0822ea90..870a86c2 100644
--- a/src/cairo-clip.c
+++ b/src/cairo-clip.c
@@ -340,7 +340,6 @@ _cairo_clip_intersect_clip (cairo_clip_t *clip,
-    }
-
-    if (clip->region) {
-	cairo_region_destroy (clip->region);
-	clip->region = NULL;
-    }
-    clip->is_region = FALSE;
+        if (clip->region) {
+            cairo_region_destroy (clip->region);
+            clip->region = NULL;
+        }
+        clip->is_region = FALSE;
+    }
